{
 "name": "rbmk_rod_drive",
 "description": "RBMK control-rod head: INSL-jacketed WIFI/PSCN/NSCN latch driving a 1px PSTN that pushes a 4px FRME rod with a VACU core down a TTAN guide; two PRTO + PRTI channel-outlet pairs and PIPE stubs at the base. 20x45 fixed.",
 "why": "Read pixel-exact from save 2001108 above channel 1 (x280-299, y60-104). Two WIFI (ch 4 = extend, ch 3 = retract) sit under INSL with NSCN/METL/PSCN chains to a PSTN at column 6; the rod body is FRME with a 2px VACU core and PTCT side bars so it slides in the TTAN guide. PRTO ch32/31/30/29 + PRTI ch30/29 at the base are the per-channel heat outlets the source uses to move core heat to the shared collector. Deviation from source: empty cells touching WIFI/PRTO/PRTI were filled with INSL (lint heat_source_uninsulated); cells where the portal must touch PIPE/METL are left as captured, so lint still reports those faces and the VACU core of the rod (it is an element rod, not a walled pump) -- both intentional. Sibling module control_rod_pstn_bank covers just the 12x24 head of this same rod (2001108 280-291,60-83); this one is the full 20x45 head+rod+portal-outlet column.",
 "source": "save 2001108, x280-299 y60-104; PSTN at (286,67)-(286,72); FRME rod (284-287,73-103); PRTO (282,85/89/97/101), PRTI (289,97/101)",
